  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed at the Beachland Ballroom in Cleveland, Ohio, on Friday, April 13, 2018 [1]. This recording, captured from the front row, documents a twenty-one-song set lasting ninety-five minutes [1]. The setlist includes “Michael Myers Resplendent,” “Oceanographer’s Choice,” and “How To Embrace A Swamp Creature” [1]. The performance features a bustout of “Going To Bolivia,” a song not played in 48 archived shows, and the mythic rare “I Know You’ve Come To Take My Toys Away” [1]. The set concludes with a five-song encore [1]. The audio quality reflects the front-row position, with low vocals due to stage monitor placement but excellent crowd sound [1]. Listeners praise the recording for its immersive energy, noting the palpable joy and audience participation [2][3][4][5]. One reviewer highlights the beautiful singing along, while another appreciates the clarity of the stage banter [3][4]. The recording is rated five stars by four listeners [1]. This is the only available recording of this specific show [1].",
